/-!
# The rational vertices of Nopert #231 (data)

Nopert #231 has fivefold symmetry about z, parallel pentagonal caps and
exactly planar quadrilaterals (27 faces: 2 pentagons, 20 triangles and 5
quads). Its twenty vertices rotate four seed vertices about the z axis in
steps of 2π/5: vertex `4k + s` is seed `s` rotated by `2πk/5` (up to
rounding). `rationalVertices` is the certified rational model (2^52
denominators, quads exactly planar in ℚ), generated by the C++ pipeline's
`codebdd` from its `nopert231_root.txt` and copied here by
`scripts/update_vertices.py`, which rewrites the bodies of `rationalVertices`
and `seedVertex` in place. Vertices are scaled to lie inside the unit sphere
(the GoodPoly invariant).

This module holds only the data (and its fast compiled form) and imports only
Mathlib, so that the modules proved directly about the data, notably the
kernel-checked tangent-cone table (`GeneratedTangentCones`), depend on
neither the certificate pipeline nor the core library. The solid model built
from these vertices (a `FivefoldSolid`, hence a `SolidModel`; its models near
the rational vertices are the pipeline's `CyclicModel`s, called `C5Model`
here) is in `Nopert231.SolidModel`.
-/

